-- title:
--   Independence over K of Hodge–Tate period coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ in the algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ (the type `PadicAlgCl p`) that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and let $\mathcal{O}_K$ be [`PadicAlgCl.ringOfIntegers p K`](def/PadicAlgCl_RingOfIntegers.html#L11), the intersection of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ with $K$. Let $G,G'$ be $p$-divisible groups of height $h$ over $\mathcal{O}_K$, i.e. systems of finite free commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal{O}_K$-algebras `level v` of rank $p^{vh}$ with surjective coalgebra transition maps whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$, and let $D$ be a Cartier duality datum between them: isomorphisms $G'.\mathrm{level}\,v \simeq \mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_K}(G.\mathrm{level}\,v,\mathcal{O}_K)$ compatible with the transition maps and multiplication by $p$. Assume $G$ has dimension $n$, in the sense that each $G.\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v$ is $\mathcal{O}_K$-isomorphic to $(\mathcal{O}_K/p^v)^n$, and let $b$ be an $\mathcal{O}_K$-basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ of `G.cotangentModule`, the submodule of $\prod_v G.\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v$ of systems compatible under the cotangent maps. Write $\mathcal{O}$ for the integral closure of $\mathcal{O}_K$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$. Let $d\alpha_j$, $j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n$, be additive maps from the Tate module of $G'(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ — the group of sequences $(x_v)$ of points with $p^v x_v = 0$ and $p\,x_{v+1} = x_v$ — to $\mathbb{C}_p$, subject to the following period estimate: for every $j$, every $y$ in that Tate module, every $v$ and every point $\psi$ of $G'$ of level $v$ with values in $\mathcal{O}$ whose image in $G'(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ at level $v$ is the $v$-th component of $y$, and every $z \in \mathcal{O} \otimes_{\mathcal{O}_K} G.\mathrm{cotangentModule}$ whose image under the $v$-th projection tensored with $\mathcal{O}$ equals the character differential $D.\mathrm{charDiff}\,\mathcal{O}\,v\,\psi$, one has $\lVert d\alpha_j(y) - (1 \otimes b^j)(z)\rVert \le p^{-v}$, where $(1\otimes b^j)(z) \in \mathcal{O} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ is viewed in $\mathbb{C}_p$. Then the $n$ functions $d\alpha_j$ from the Tate module to $\mathbb{C}_p$ are linearly independent over $K$.
--
--   This is Proposition 11 of Tate's paper on $p$-divisible groups, in the generality of a base $\mathcal{O}_K$ for a finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}_p$: the coordinates, in a basis of the cotangent module, of the Hodge–Tate period map on the Tate module of the Cartier dual are $K$-linearly independent as $\mathbb{C}_p$-valued functions. It feeds the construction of a $K$-linearly independent Galois-equivariant family of $\mathbb{C}_p$-valued functionals on the Tate module, from which the Hodge–Tate decomposition of the Tate module of a $p$-divisible group is obtained.
